// RHYTHM BANKRUPTCY — HOSTILE TAKEOVER — one song: what it plays, how it is arranged, how it sounds.
//
// RHYTHM BANKRUPTCY as big-room house — THE BANGER. A game alternate of rhythm,
// selectable from the dev menu (GAME ALTERNATES) and on the desk. Nothing replaces
// the live song.
// 
// Both of the original's figures, and its own key lifts. The ARP (cycle one, the
// lead the coin fills were authored against) owns the intro, the builds and the
// breakdown; the POPCORN HOOK (cycle two — six staccato eighths and a beat of
// nothing) is the drop, on an electric grand doubled by a plain square, over a
// pumping supersaw and an off-beat bass. The doo-wop turnaround is kept cell for
// cell (C Am F G, the ii, the climb, the arrival) at a chord a bar. Drop two is a
// whole step up, with the arp back as a pluck counter-line; after a false ending,
// drop three lands in E with both figures at once — C, D, E, the lift rhythm.js
// makes itself.
// 
//   1–4    intro — filtered pump, the arp on the grand (the cabinet-screen loop)
//   5–8    build — the filter opens, snare roll, riser, the arp's climbing tail
//   9–24   DROP ONE (C) — the Popcorn hook, pump, off-beat bass, impact and crash
//   25–28  breakdown — the arp re-harmonised: Am7 Fmaj7 Bbmaj7#11 G7sus4, choir
//   29–32  build — the hook held in C while the chords climb to A7
//   33–48  DROP TWO (D) — + arp pluck, rolling bass; a saw doubles the hook 8vb at 41
//   49–52  false ending — the grand alone on the arrival phrase, then into B7
//   53–60  DROP THREE (E) — the double drop: hook, arp, saw, screamer, ride
//   61–64  turnaround — the arp walks E, C, D, G7; the loop returns to bar 5
// 
// THE BEAT CABINET'S CLOCK IS KEPT. 124 BPM straight, 4/4, phrases of four bars
// from bar 1, and the kick on every quarter of every bar — the beat charts are laid
// off Audio.songBeat() mod 16 and the hero's jump was measured in beats at 124. The
// loop is bars 5–64: 60 bars, the length the original loops, a whole number of
// 16-beat chart loops, so a wrap or a retry's beat-jump lands every hole on the same
// beat of the music.
// 
// 64 bars at 124. Written by work/local/_rhythm-remix-hostile-takeover.mjs
// through work/local/_remix-lib.mjs; re-running it rewrites this file.
//
// SPOT FX (1 Oct 2026, work/local/_spot-fx-stops.mjs): the false ending on bar 49 cuts the drop's tails; the grand, its pad and the four-on-the-floor play on.
//
// SPOT FX — MORE (1 Oct 2026, work/local/_spot-fx-more.mjs): the whole mix opens an eighth at a time over the build (5–8).
//
// The music below is the composition. Everything under THE DESK WRITES BELOW HERE
// is written by `npm run mixer` and will be rewritten on every save — put notes
